# house-domains.txt.example — the mail domains that belong to YOU (the house), and nobody else.
#
# Copy to $YMIR_HOME/hodd/identity/house-domains.txt (private, never in this repo) and fill in
# your own. One domain per line; `#` starts a comment.
#
# Read at run time by two wards, so the repository never spells a domain of yours (RULES/04):
#
#   bin/gates/guards/identity-guard.sh   a commit may be AUTHORED as <agent>@<one of these>
#                                        (the house's agent identities), and nothing else is;
#   bin/records/developers.sh            an author whose address is on one of these is shown
#                                        as a house identity, while a person's mailbox is masked.
#
# A home that declares none is not an error: both fall back to the generic forms only
# (`@ymir`, `@ymir.local`, `@users.noreply.github.com`), which is what a fresh fleet wants.

example.org
example.com
